{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Mobile: space fixes for the cart drawer.

  1. The "Your Cart (n items)" bar stops sticking.
     pg-drawer pins it with `.pg-cart-top{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:6}`. It
     permanently eats part of the panel and rides over whatever scrolls beneath
     it -- on a phone it sat on top of the "Add & Save More" heading, on desktop
     it covers the drawer logo and free-shipping pill. It now scrolls with the
     list, keeping its background and rule so it still reads as the panel header.

  2. The totals pane gets shorter.
     `.sticky-in-panel` stacks shipping protection, the savings breakdown, the
     totals, the trust row, the checkout button and the payment icons. Each is
     fine on its own; together they take more than half the screen.

     Nothing is removed. Everything is tightened: smaller paddings and gaps,
     one step down in type on the secondary rows, and payment icons at 26x17
     instead of 36x23. The one exception is the shipping-protection subtitle
     ("Protect your order against loss or damage in transit"), which is hidden
     below 760px -- the label, price and toggle all remain, and that sentence is
     a full wrapped line on a phone.

     The total and the checkout button are deliberately left large: they are
     what the pane is for.

  3. The pane stops being frozen (see the block below for why).

  The header bar is unpinned at every width -- on desktop it was covering the
  drawer logo and free-shipping pill as the panel scrolled. The pane compaction
  and unpinning stay under 760px, where the height actually matters; the 490px
  desktop drawer keeps its roomier spacing and its pinned pane.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
/* 1. header bar scrolls away, all widths */
#cart .pg-cart-top{
  position:static !important;
  top:auto !important;
  z-index:auto !important
}

@media (max-width:760px){
  /* 3. the pane stops being frozen.
     Even after the compaction below, the pinned pane measured ~364px tall once
     the shipping-protection row, savings breakdown, totals, trust strip,
     checkout button and payment icons were stacked -- and the upsell panel
     above it pushed the item list down to y=502 on an 844px phone. The pane
     started at y=456, so it covered the top of the list: not one cart item was
     fully visible without scrolling.

     Two symptoms came out of that. The cart looked squished, and a 24px strip
     of cart peeked out below the pane -- the drawer carries an inline
     `padding-bottom:34px` set by the theme's own script, while the pane sticks
     at `bottom:-10px`, so it came to rest 24px short of the screen edge with
     list showing through the difference.

     Unpinning puts the pane at the bottom of the drawer, where it reads as the
     end of the cart. Nothing floats, so nothing peeks out underneath it, and
     the item list gets the full height rather than a slot above the pane
     (measured: 342px of list, first item fully visible, versus none before).

     Trade-off worth knowing: checkout is now reached by scrolling to the end of
     the drawer rather than always being on screen. */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel{
    position:static !important;
    bottom:auto !important;
    box-shadow:none !important
  }

  /* 2. compact the pane */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel{padding-top:3px !important;padding-bottom:5px !important}

  /* shipping protection: single line, smaller icon */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp{margin:2px 0 5px !important;padding:6px 9px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-ic{width:24px !important;height:24px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-ic svg{width:14px !important;height:14px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-t b{font-size:12.5px !important;line-height:1.25 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-t small{display:none !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-price{font-size:12.5px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-sw{transform:scale(.9);transform-origin:right center}

  /* savings breakdown */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sav{margin:2px 0 5px !important;padding:6px 9px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sav-r{font-size:12px !important;line-height:1.4 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sav-t{margin-top:3px !important;padding-top:4px !important;font-size:12.5px !important}

  /* totals: subtotal and discount rows tighten, the Total holds its weight */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .l4tt{margin:1px 0 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .l4tt li{font-size:12.5px !important;padding:0 !important;line-height:1.35 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .l4tt li.pg-drow,#cart .sticky-in-panel .l4tt li.pg-drow *{font-size:12.5px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .l4tt li.pg-tt,#cart .sticky-in-panel .l4tt li.pg-tt *{font-size:15px !important}

  /* trust strip */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .nc-dtrust{margin:2px 0 !important;padding:0 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .nc-dtrust span{font-size:10px !important}

  /* checkout stays a full-size target */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel form.f8vl{margin:2px 0 0 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel button[name="checkout"]{padding:12px 16px !important}

  /* payment icons: one tight row */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .l4pm{margin:4px 0 0 !important;gap:5px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .l4pm li{padding:2px 4px !important;border-radius:6px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .l4pm svg{width:26px !important;height:17px !important}
}
</style>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Cart Mobile", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
